    "problems": [
      {
        "category": "doc_contract_interpreter_coupling",
        "summary": "A valid sealed documentation report read as stale under a different Python, costing two reviewer must-fix items and one wrong diagnosis.",
        "evidence": "doc_inventory.python_units digests ast.dump output, which changed between 3.10 and 3.13: identical tree gives 7230056ee9 under 3.10.19 and 8086e2cb under 3.13.12 across all 57 inventoried .py files, with every file byte-identical. Review B diagnosed it; review A reported it as a must-fix, eliminated every tree-side cause and stated it could not root-cause the refusal. Reproduced again on the re-sealed report.",
        "minutes_lost": 45
      },
      {
        "category": "post_approval_edit_invalidates_evidence",
        "summary": "Arch took a reviewer's non-blocking cosmetic doc fix after both approvals, staling the seal; reverting then stranded a reviewer signature and dropped the approval count to 1 of 2.",
        "evidence": "One line in docs/verification_matrix.md moved doc_contract check from valid:true to 'report is stale' on a report both reviewers had confirmed. Reverting restored the seal but moved the signature from 47f925ff back to fba754589b, so final_verification reported '1 independent approvals; 2 required'. One reviewer re-affirmation turn spent. Review B then established the edit never entered its review at all - only its end-of-turn signature sample.",
        "minutes_lost": 25
      },
      {
        "category": "glob_discovery_enrolls_out_of_scope_case",
        "summary": "A new verification input directory was silently enrolled in a test that could not judge it, and the scientific suite failed at final verification after five focused passes and two approvals.",
        "evidence": "tests/runoff/lab_sea_runoff_timing_check.py globbed input.rnof_*; lab_sea/input.rnof_sp_const matched a check that models only the dense pkg/exf path, giving FAIL 'monitor output has 48 runoff records'. Review A measured the cause: exf_monitor.F:190 writes _runoff stats only when runofffile is non-blank (240 lines dense, 0 sparse). Cost one correction round plus a failed 33-command suite run.",
        "minutes_lost": 75
      },
      {
        "category": "overstated_partial_suite_result",
        "summary": "Arch characterised the failed suite run as 'everything else passed' when the runner had halted at the first failure and 7 of 33 commands never executed, including six no-change experiments that are a completion criterion.",
        "evidence": "The log has 26 COMMAND lines of 33 configured. Commands 27-33 did not run: the --mpi 2 timing check and 1D_ocean_ice_column, seaice_obcs, offline_exf_seaice, seaice_itd, isomip, tutorial_advection_in_gyre. Review B enumerated them and rejected the characterisation; the claim had also been reported to the owner twice before correction.",
        "minutes_lost": 15
      },
      {
        "category": "provider_api_error_kills_agent_turn",
        "summary": "Bob's turn terminated on 'the response stopped arriving' twice, so correction round 2 has no completed implementer footer.",
        "evidence": "Two task notifications with status failed mid-item. Both resumed on the same identity without redoing work, but the latest bob completion event is round 1 while the candidate contains round-2 edits. That work is evidenced by Arch and both reviewers independently, not by its implementer.",
        "minutes_lost": 20
      }
    ],
    "solutions": [
      {
        "problem": 0,
        "action": "filed",
        "issue": "TEAM-DOCCONTRACT-AST-DUMP-DIGEST-001"
      },
      {
        "problem": 1,
        "action": "fixed",
        "reference": "lessons_learned.md LL-006 and lessons_learned_evidence.md",
        "reason": "Recorded as a lesson with its counterexample: edits to open_issues.md, lessons_learned.md and the ESX ledger leave both the seal and the signature untouched, verified after each edit, so those are the safe places to record a late finding. The durable rule is to route post-approval findings to non-inventoried files."
      },
      {
        "problem": 2,
        "action": "fixed",
        "reference": "tests/runoff/lab_sea_runoff_timing_check.py::sparse_case and LL-008",
        "reason": "The fix is an enforced scope predicate rather than a habit: sparse_case discriminates on configuration intent, reports an out-of-scope match as SKIP with its reason and owning issue, keeps it out of the JSON results array, and a guard makes an all-skip run exit non-zero. Verified by execution, including review A driving discovery to confirm the guard really fails."
      },
      {
        "problem": 3,
        "action": "fixed",
        "reference": "devel-loop/loop_state/issue-done.json verification.round2_failed_run",
        "reason": "The closeout record now carries the accurate accounting - 26 executed, 25 passed, 1 failed, 7 not run and named individually as unmeasured rather than passing - plus a correction_note stating the earlier claim was false. The gap itself closed by measurement in the passing re-run, not by assertion."
      },
      {
        "problem": 4,
        "action": "deferred",
        "issue": "TEAM-DOCCONTRACT-AST-DUMP-DIGEST-001",
        "reason": "Provider transport failures are outside this project's control and the existing resume path worked without losing work, so no project-side change is warranted; recorded here so that a recurrence pattern across iterations becomes visible rather than being absorbed silently each time."
      }
