    "confirmations": [
      {
        "category": "distinct_reviewer_questions",
        "summary": "The one standing rule worked: the two reviewers found disjoint defect sets with no overlap.",
        "evidence": "Review A owned placement and conservation and proved the applied field bitwise identical over all 6144 cs32 cells plus a bijective ownership map; review B owned refusals, MPI safety and claim integrity and proved the cross-rank reduction with two cases the suite never had. Neither duplicated the other, and each caught items the other did not."
      },
      {
        "category": "reviewer_executed_own_check",
        "summary": "Requiring approval to rest on something the reviewer executed, not on the implementer's evidence, found what the configured oracle could not.",
        "evidence": "Review A built a cell-exact oracle rather than re-running the sealed suite, and with it measured that a cross-facet one-cell move passes compare_results.sh at exactly 10 of 10 required digits - zero margin - which the digit threshold cannot see because mass is conserved. That became RUNOFF-033 and LL-007."
      },
      {
        "category": "final_verification_catches_unassigned_scope",
        "summary": "A final verification owned by someone other than the implementer and reviewers caught a defect in nobody's assignment.",
        "evidence": "All three agents explicitly recorded not running the scientific suite. It failed on command 26. Explicit limits made the gap visible in the record but did not prevent it reaching final verification, which is the argument for the final owner running the whole suite rather than trusting the union of focused runs."
      }
    ],
    "carry_forward": [
      "RUNOFF-033 owns promoting review A's cell-exact placement oracle into the configured suite plus an init-time target_lon/target_lat check; until then placement has no configured test with margin.",
      "docs/verification_matrix.md understates its own coverage ('the end state of the run' where compare_results.sh compares every monitor line) and still has a dangling 'the two not seen rows' cross-reference; both deferred under LL-006 to the next issue that edits the file.",
      "lab_sea_runoff_timing_check.py::check_case reports monitor times as 'runoff records', which would mislead on a truncated dense run even though the sparse trigger is gone.",
      "RUNOFF-017 gains review B's cross-rank global-count refusal oracle (land_rank1_only, land_both_ranks); its scratch receipt is git-ignored, so re-derive from the issue text.",
      "Still unexecuted after this issue: the exch2 fold and long-line placement branches, maskInC = 0, kTopC != 0 (never compiled - no experiment builds both rnf and shelfice), blank exch2 tiles, multi-threaded runs, non-constant records, LLC."
